// rustc nll/issue-53040.rs — upstream captured variable cannot escape `FnMut` body
// imported batch B167 @ da5114692c9ebe46b869488c5f34f92eb10b98c1 (rust 1.100.0)
// shelf: fail — CLOSED 2026-08-28 by the AddrOf capture-mutability read.
// ⚠ RIGHT VERDICT, DIFFERENT REASON, AND THAT IS RECORDED RATHER THAN GLOSSED.
// Upstream refuses this as E0521 "captured variable cannot escape `FnMut`
// closure body". We refuse it because `&mut v` is now recorded as a MUT
// capture loan held by `f`, and `let r = f()` deposits provenance on every
// capture of the callee (collect_ref_sources_paths' ClosureCall arm — a
// closure body is never summarised), which conflicts. The escape channel
// itself is still unbuilt; see the round report for the constructed legal
// program that same imprecision refuses, and its control.
// port of rust tests/ui/nll/issue-53040.rs
// the FnMut closure body yields a &mut of its own capture, which escapes.
// rustc: E0507/E0521 captured variable cannot escape `FnMut` closure body.
package issue_53040;
fn main() -> i32 {
    let mut v: i64 = 0i64;
    let f = || -> &mut i64 { return &mut v; };
    let r: &mut i64 = f();
    *r = 1i64;
    return 0i32;
}
